      "httpStatus": 200,
      "latencyMs": 906,
      "answer": "Deep determinants of growth are the underlying factors that help explain why some countries are rich and others poor. In this course, they are identified as institutions, geography, culture, and openness. Classical growth theory frames the problem by focusing on constraints like diminishing returns, the Malthusian trap, and the role of land, while modern approaches use these deep determinants to explain persistent differences in growth.",
